# Line-ending policy.
#
# The bridge artefact (bridge/dist/tray-bridge.js) is generated by a script that
# parses its sources line by line with anchored regular expressions. Those
# expressions are written for LF. A Windows checkout that converts LF to CRLF
# leaves a trailing "\r" on every line, the parsers stop matching, and
# `node scripts/build-bridge.mjs --check` fails even though no source changed.
# That is exactly what happened on the first CI run.
#
# So: every text file in this repository is stored and checked out with LF.
# Do not override this for source files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch them, never diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.tgz binary
*.asar binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
